{"t": 5.675, "dir": "in", "msg": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"contents": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "### Keyword *Probe Catalog Endpoint*\n\n#### Arguments: \n\n| | | | |\n|:--|:--|:--|:--|\n| `path`|   |  |  |\n| `expected_status`|   | = | `200` |\n\n#### Documentation:\nGETs `path` from the catalog API and returns the response.\n\n"}, "range": {"start": {"line": 6, "character": 16}, "end": {"line": 6, "character": 38}}}}}
{"t": 5.675, "dir": "out", "msg": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "method": "textDocument/hover", "params": {"textDocument": {"uri": "file://~/workspace/rf-mcp-robotcode/experiments/robotcode-remote/round3/agent_lsp/probe/p_pull/tests/shop.robot"}, "position": {"line": 7, "character": 8}}}}
{"t": 5.682, "dir": "in", "msg": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"contents": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "### Keyword *Should Be Equal As Integers*\n\n#### Arguments: \n\n| | | | |\n|:--|:--|:--|:--|\n| `first`| : `object` |  |  |\n| `second`| : `object` |  |  |\n| `msg`| : `str` \\| `None` | = | `${None}` |\n| `values`| : `bool` | = | `${True}` |\n| `base`| : `int` \\| `None` | = | `${None}` |\n\n#### Documentation:\nFails if objects are unequal after converting them to integers.\n\nArgs:\n    first: The first value to compare.\n    second: The second value to compare.\n    msg: The custom error message.\n    values: If true, compared values are added to the custom error message.\n    base: Optional base to use in integer conversion.\n\nSee [Convert To Integer] for information how to convert integers from\nother bases than 10 by using the `base` argument and `0b/0o/0x` prefixes.\n\nSee the [Controlling failure messages] section for information about\noverriding the default failure message with `msg` and `values` arguments.\n\nExamples:\n```robotframework\n*** Test Cases ***\nShould be equal as integers\n    Should Be Equal As Integers    42        ${42}    Error message\n    Should Be Equal As Integers    ABCD      abcd     base=16\n    Should Be Equal As Integers    0b1011    11\n```\n\nAn alternative to using [Should Be Equal As Integers] is using\nthe [Should Be Equal] keyword with `type` and `types` arguments\nthat support type conversion and validation."}, "range": {"start": {"line": 7, "character": 4}, "end": {"line": 7, "character": 31}}}}}
{"t": 5.682, "dir": "out", "msg": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/didOpen", "params": {"textDocument": {"uri": "file://~/workspace/rf-mcp-robotcode/experiments/robotcode-remote/round3/agent_lsp/probe/p_pull/resources/shop.resource", "languageId": "robotframework", "version": 1, "text": "*** Settings ***\nDocumentation     Page objects for the demo shop. Use ONLY these keywords in tests.\nLibrary           Browser\nLibrary           RequestsLibrary\n\n*** Variables ***\n${SHOP_URL}         http://127.0.0.1:8765/shop.html\n${API_URL}          http://127.0.0.1:8765\n${FINDER_INPUT}     css=input#product-finder\n${HIT_ROWS}         css=ul#hits > li\n\n*** Keywords ***\nLaunch Storefront\n    [Documentation]    Opens a fresh headless browser on the shop start page.\n    [Arguments]    ${headless}=True\n    New Browser    chromium    headless=${headless}\n    New Page    ${SHOP_URL}\n\nType Into Product Finder\n    [Documentation]    Types ``term`` into the product finder box and submits it with Enter.\n    [Arguments]    ${term}\n    Fill Text    ${FINDER_INPUT}    ${term}\n    Keyboard Key    press    Enter\n\nHit Count Should Be\n    [Documentation]    Asserts that exactly ``expected`` result rows are shown.\n    [Arguments]    ${expected}\n    Get Element Count    ${HIT_ROWS}    ==    ${expected}\n\nProbe Catalog Endpoint\n    [Documentation]    GETs ``path`` from the catalog API and returns the response.\n    [Arguments]    ${path}    ${expected_status}=200\n    Create Session    catalog    ${API_URL}\n    ${resp}=    GET On Session    catalog    ${path}    expected_status=${expected_status}\n    RETURN    ${resp}\n"}}}}
